advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          scope_remove
description   "Remove theory-name patterns from the resource scope.
              Patterns are removed literally (the exact strings
              previously added), not by re-matching — removing
              \"HOL-Library.*\" removes that pattern, not individual
              theories it matched. The implicit scope members (loaded
              theories, active REPLs, named resources) are not
              removable this way; unload_theory / repl_remove govern
              those. Replies with the remaining scope."
              (the literal-removal semantics is this plan's decision
              — matching-based removal would need set subtraction
              over patterns, which has no clean meaning; pin it
              here, spec's scoping section stays compatible.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "patterns": {"type": "array",
                              "items": {"type": "string"}}},
               "required": ["patterns"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

